    affiliation: >-
      Yıldız Technical University, Faculty of Mechanical Engineering, Department of Mechatronics Engineering, Istanbul, Türkiye
repository-code: "https://github.com/abdulhamidbatayhi123/ai-kinetics-discoverability"
abstract: >-
  A pre-registered computational study of when equation-discovery methods recover the kinetic law of an adsorption column from its outlet and profile data. Ground truth comes from a verified finite-difference solver (imported from the Paper 1 archive, doi:10.5281/zenodo.23323685). Sparse regression in weak and strong forms, exact best-subset selection, ensembles, errors-in-variables regression, symbolic regression and a neural network in the column model are compared, over a grid of Damkoehler number, Peclet number, noise, isotherm error and three observation models, against profile-likelihood identifiability of the rate constant. The pre-registration (PREREG_P2_discoverability.md) was frozen before any method ran on the grid; amendments A1 to A4 preceded the grid, A5 was made while it ran, and A6 and A7 (implementation corrections, RETRACTIONS_P2 B87, B89, B90) after the first verdicts, with every earlier result file kept. The commit history is kept here.
keywords:
  - equation discovery
  - adsorption kinetics
  - identifiability
  - sparse regression
  - symbolic regression
  - universal differential equations
  - metal-organic frameworks
  - pre-registration
